.TH AUTH "1" "October 2026" "auth" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
authpass \- Create and manage passwords
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B authpass 
[\fI--cipher blowfish|md5\fR]
[\fI--file filename\fR]
[\fI--password password\fR] 
[\fI--rounds count\fR] 
realm username roles...

.SH DESCRIPTION
The authpass program creates authentication passwords for Appweb. It should be used to create passwords
for the "config" or "app" authentication stores. If using the "config" authentication store, use the "--file" option
to specify the name of the password file. 

.RS 5
authpass --file auth.conf --password pass1 example.com joshua administrator buyer
.RE

If using the "app" authentication store, omit the "--file" option and the password will be displayed to the standard output.

.RS 5
authpass --password pass1 example.com joshua administrator buyer
.RE

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\--cipher blowfish|md5\fR 
Specifies the cipher to use to hash the password. Default is blowfish. Blowfish is substantially more secure.
MD5 must be used for digest authentication.
.TP
\fB\--password password\fR 
Specifies a password to use to for the user. Omit this option to be prompted for the password: a password on the
command line is visible to other local users and is kept in the shell history.
.TP
\fB\--file filename\fR 
Update the specified password configuration file.
.TP
\fB\--rounds count\fR 
Number of Blowfish hashing rounds. Each round adds cost to every login and to every password guess made by an
attacker who obtains the password file. The default is set when Appweb is built (ME_MPR_BF_ROUNDS). Use fewer rounds
on very slow devices where login latency matters, or more where it does not. Existing passwords keep the rounds they
were created with.
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
The authpass program is used to create and manage user passwords.
Appweb uses the same authorization file and format for Basic, Digest and form authentication. This simplifies administration.
Keep the password file readable only by the server account.
